      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, it seems you were automatically added for review before I\u0027ve finished uploading all the related CLs. I\u0027ll reply again once they\u0027re uploaded. I have shared a relevant document with you.\n\nThe usual signature-based methodology configured via mac_permissions.xml doesn\u0027t suit WebView\u0027s needs very well:\n\n- WebView providers are currently defined via a config_webview_packages.xml resource, which only sometimes specifies signatures. System-installed WebViews don\u0027t have signature enforcement.\n- config_webview_packages.xml as a resource can be overridden (particularly for GMS builds), complicating maintenance of mac_permissions.xml.\n- Debuggable builds of Android don\u0027t enforce signature checks for WebView providers, in order to ease development. The mac_permissions.xml approach doesn\u0027t have such a distinction for debuggable builds.\n- There are some additional (minor) restrictions on what can be considered a WebView provider, which aren\u0027t captured by package name and signature alone.",
